  "details": "Say you have the following type of setup:\n\nRoot constraint\nIs a parent of: Child constraint\nIs a parent of: Contact receiver\n\nAnd both constraints are active.\nThe SDK does not seem to take the offset resulting from Child constraint into account when calculating the Contact receiver's position. This is clearly visible using the contact overlay in the VRChat client.\nTesting in Unity with Lyuma's emulator, the Contact receiver's gizmo will DISPLAY in the correct location (affected by both constraints). However, it will still activate as if it was in the wrong location where the SDK assumes it should be (affected only by Root constraint).",
